      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess this looks more readable than #if ... #endif but it\u0027s also less obvious that this member is conditionally included. This style also makes a non-array member look like an array. Does it also work for real arrays?\n\nHow about using a wrapper? That is, we write:\n\n  int foo INCLUDE_IF(CONFIG_FOO);\n\nwhere\n\n  #define INCLUDE_IF(x) [IS_ENABLED_IF(x)]\n\nThen, we can keep the nice message of IS_ENABLED (option#3).\n\nWhat do other projects do?",
